  "body": "  A certain function has its local linearization at given by .   What are the values of and ? Why?    Estimate the value of .    Suppose that and you know that for . Is your estimate in (b) too large or too small?    Suppose that for . Use this fact and the additional information above to sketch an accurate graph of near . Include a sketch of in your work.           and .     .    Too large.               Since the value and slope of the tangent line match the value and slope of the function at the point of tangency, we know and .    Using the local linearization, .    Since for , we know that is concave down for . This means to the left of the point of tangency at , the tangent line lies above the curve, and thus the estimate in (b) is too large.    In the following figure, we see a possible function that matches the value and slope of the tangent line at the point and that is concave down to the left of and concave up to the right.         "
