  "body": "  A potato is placed in an oven, and the potato's temperature (in degrees Fahrenheit) at various points in time is taken and recorded in the following table. Time is measured in minutes.   Temperature data for the potato.                            Use a central difference to estimate . Use this estimate as needed in subsequent questions.    Find the local linearization to the function at the point where .    Determine an estimate for by employing the local linearization.    Do you think your estimate in (c) is too large or too small? Why?           degrees per minute.     .     degrees F.    Overestimate.          The central difference approximation with gives degrees per minute.    The local linearization at is .    Using the linearization from (b), degrees F.    Since the values of given in the table appear to be increasing at a decreasing rate near , it follows that the graph of is concave down near . This implies that the graph of (the tangent line to at lies above the graph of . Therefore, the approximation given in part (c) is probably an overestimate.      "
