  "body": "  Sand is being dumped off a conveyor belt onto a pile in such a way that the pile forms in the shape of a cone whose radius is always equal to its height. Assuming that the sand is being dumped at a rate of cubic feet per minute, how fast is the height of the pile changing when there are cubic feet on the pile?     feet per minute.    We can draw a figure similar to Figure and let be the height of the pile at time and the pile's base radius. Given that cubic feet per minute, we want to know .  We first relate and . We know that , as well as that for every time, , the height and radius are equal so . Thus, Differentiating both sides of this equation with respect to  . We note that at the instant , , so and therefore . Recall also that . Applying all of this information at the instant in the equation that relates and , we have . Thus, feet per minute.   "
